WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.236 --> 00:00:01.421
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.421 --> 00:00:05.011
Today's message is pursue perfection

00:00:05.011 --> 00:00:07.220
over you, Benedict Cumberbatch.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.654
(rooster crowing)

00:00:09.654 --> 00:00:12.147
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:12.147 --> 00:00:14.853
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:00:14.853 --> 00:00:18.862
♫ I wake every morning

00:00:18.862 --> 00:00:21.477
- You can never perfect what we do.

00:00:21.477 --> 00:00:24.112
There is no way, I've
never met anyone who goes,

00:00:24.112 --> 00:00:24.956
"That's perfection."

00:00:24.956 --> 00:00:28.014
I mean, to an audience,
outside of your work,

00:00:28.014 --> 00:00:29.344
people can think that that's the only way

00:00:29.344 --> 00:00:30.699
they'd ever want to see that part played

00:00:30.699 --> 00:00:31.821
or that moment done, whatever,

00:00:31.821 --> 00:00:34.272
but as an actor, and
this isn't mock humility,

00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:36.754
I think it just go for
all art forms, really,

00:00:36.754 --> 00:00:39.185
that the whole point is
perfection is unachievable.

00:00:39.185 --> 00:00:42.681
So, it's that constant
pursuit of the unobtainable,

00:00:42.681 --> 00:00:45.379
which is kind of magic, really.

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:49.345
And, should keep us kind
of motivated to try better,

00:00:49.345 --> 00:00:52.091
it's the Beckett thing,
fail again, fail better.

00:00:52.091 --> 00:00:54.478
- My unhealthy relationship
with perfection

00:00:54.478 --> 00:00:58.295
cost me $40 million
when I was 22 years old.

00:00:58.295 --> 00:01:01.192
I had my software
company, we were growing,

00:01:01.192 --> 00:01:03.494
and we had this big vision
for what we could do.

00:01:03.494 --> 00:01:04.941
We had this big business plan for

00:01:04.941 --> 00:01:06.887
the types of companies that we could help.

00:01:06.887 --> 00:01:11.054
And the flaw was, I wanted
to have the perfect plan.

00:01:12.131 --> 00:01:16.007
And I spent an entire
summer working on the plan,

00:01:16.007 --> 00:01:18.649
buildin' the plan, researchin' the plan,

00:01:18.649 --> 00:01:23.103
and zero time actually
trying to execute the plan.

00:01:23.103 --> 00:01:24.928
And, there came a time when I was 22

00:01:24.928 --> 00:01:26.977
whe we had the opportunity
to sell our company.

00:01:26.977 --> 00:01:28.986
And a big player was coming in.

00:01:28.986 --> 00:01:31.852
They raised a huge
fund, like $800 million,

00:01:31.852 --> 00:01:33.867
to go out and buy companies.

00:01:33.867 --> 00:01:36.008
And they were looking at
our biggest competitor.

00:01:36.008 --> 00:01:37.750
And then they started looking at us.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.374
And we were late to the party.

00:01:39.374 --> 00:01:41.735
We were a late throw-in.

00:01:41.735 --> 00:01:42.960
And we weren't ready.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.988
But we got to be number two,
it was between the two of us.

00:01:45.988 --> 00:01:49.141
And they chose our competitor over us.

00:01:49.141 --> 00:01:50.157
They chose our competitor

00:01:50.157 --> 00:01:52.610
because they had more
of the plan worked out.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.163
They were executing harder.

00:01:54.163 --> 00:01:58.600
Where, for us, we had some
of the plan worked out,

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.136
but we hadn't done enough.

00:02:00.136 --> 00:02:01.774
And so, we lost that deal,

00:02:01.774 --> 00:02:04.322
and they bought our
competitor for $40 million.

00:02:04.322 --> 00:02:05.720
And that stung.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:06.941
That hurt.

00:02:06.941 --> 00:02:10.484
That was a big loss for me,
I took that really hard.

00:02:10.484 --> 00:02:12.901
And I realized if we just did

00:02:14.224 --> 00:02:16.895
a better job of executing our plan,

00:02:16.895 --> 00:02:21.016
if we didn't care about
reaching perfection,

00:02:21.016 --> 00:02:23.280
if that wasn't our sole goal,

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:26.265
then maybe we would have got that deal.

00:02:26.265 --> 00:02:28.957
That regret, that feeling like,

00:02:28.957 --> 00:02:30.342
If I did things a little differently,

00:02:30.342 --> 00:02:32.160
I probably could have got that deal.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.850
And so, perfection is this funny thing.

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:36.828
Perfection is a great
thing to try to go after,

00:02:36.828 --> 00:02:39.186
to try to reach, to
always try to get better,

00:02:39.186 --> 00:02:43.399
but not let it hold you
back from doing something.

00:02:43.399 --> 00:02:46.151
This plagues so many entrepreneurs.

00:02:46.151 --> 00:02:47.592
So many wanna-be entrepreneurs.

00:02:47.592 --> 00:02:49.196
You have an idea for what you want to do,

00:02:49.196 --> 00:02:50.211
and so you're planning, planning,

00:02:50.211 --> 00:02:52.766
planning, planning, planning,
and then you never do,

00:02:52.766 --> 00:02:54.492
and then you miss your window.

00:02:54.492 --> 00:02:57.270
You miss your window because
that opportunity has passed,

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:00.078
or some life event comes
up and distracts you,

00:03:00.078 --> 00:03:02.454
or some other thing happens.

00:03:02.454 --> 00:03:04.420
Like, you miss your window, it happened,

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.299
and then you see somebody else go out

00:03:06.299 --> 00:03:07.702
and make tons of money and have

00:03:07.702 --> 00:03:10.452
a huge impact that was your idea.

00:03:12.101 --> 00:03:14.309
And you can't blame that person.

00:03:14.309 --> 00:03:15.796
The only person you can blame is yourself

00:03:15.796 --> 00:03:17.828
because you didn't do anything about it,

00:03:17.828 --> 00:03:20.389
'cause you spent so long
planning and planning

00:03:20.389 --> 00:03:23.422
and planning to get the perfect plan.

00:03:23.422 --> 00:03:26.077
Understand that there is no
such thing as a perfect plan.

00:03:26.077 --> 00:03:27.677
There is no such thing
as a perfect product,

00:03:27.677 --> 00:03:29.812
there's no such thing
as a perfect service.

00:03:29.812 --> 00:03:32.595
If you ever hit perfection,
go out and quit,

00:03:32.595 --> 00:03:35.403
and go do something else,
'cause you've hit the highest.

00:03:35.403 --> 00:03:36.622
It's never perfect.

00:03:36.622 --> 00:03:38.638
And, that's also part of the fun.

00:03:38.638 --> 00:03:42.931
Like, the struggle and the
strive to hit perfection

00:03:42.931 --> 00:03:46.303
needs to be the game, not
just hitting perfection.

00:03:46.303 --> 00:03:49.495
The struggle and the drive
to get better at what you do,

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.138
to make better videos,
to make a better service,

00:03:52.138 --> 00:03:56.132
to have your customers
love you more is the game,

00:03:56.132 --> 00:03:59.027
is what you should be loving
doing and working on improving.

00:03:59.027 --> 00:04:02.328
And so, yes, you want to
try to pursue perfection,

00:04:02.328 --> 00:04:04.595
understand you're never going to hit it,

00:04:04.595 --> 00:04:08.100
and that's not only okay, it's great.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.224
It's great to continue to have this goal

00:04:10.224 --> 00:04:11.318
that you're shooting towards,

00:04:11.318 --> 00:04:15.159
'cause once you hit a goal, you fall off.

00:04:15.159 --> 00:04:16.505
You get depressed.

00:04:16.505 --> 00:04:19.045
And, so, don't let that
pursuit of perfection

00:04:19.045 --> 00:04:20.962
prevent you from taking action.

00:04:20.962 --> 00:04:22.393
It's both.

00:04:22.393 --> 00:04:25.210
It's take action and make it better.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:27.127
It's start and improve.

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.247
Don't let that pursuit of perfection

00:04:30.247 --> 00:04:33.593
prevent you from getting
started on your path.

00:04:33.593 --> 00:04:37.232
Don't make that $40 million
mistake that I made,

00:04:37.232 --> 00:04:39.188
and I learned my lesson on,

00:04:39.188 --> 00:04:41.745
and I'm hopefully never
going to make again.

00:04:41.745 --> 00:04:44.267
So the question of the
day today is I'm curious

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:46.228
are you a perfectionist and has it

00:04:46.228 --> 00:04:48.707
held you back in your
life or your business?

00:04:48.707 --> 00:04:50.069
Super curious to find out.

00:04:50.069 --> 00:04:51.233
Leave it down in the comments below

00:04:51.233 --> 00:04:53.044
and we'll join in the discussion.

00:04:53.044 --> 00:04:55.223
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Miguel Camara.

00:04:55.223 --> 00:04:56.763
Miguel, thank you so much for pickin' up

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.931
a copy of my book, Your One Word.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.572
I really, really appreciate the support

00:05:00.572 --> 00:05:02.101
and hope you're enjoying the read.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.588
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:05:03.588 --> 00:05:04.748
I believe in you.

00:05:04.748 --> 00:05:06.667
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:08.525
and whatever your one word is.

00:05:08.525 --> 00:05:10.008
And I'll see you again tomorrow morning.

00:05:10.008 --> 00:05:12.391
For another shot of espresso.

00:05:12.391 --> 00:05:14.867
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:14.867 --> 00:05:17.739
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:05:17.739 --> 00:05:18.572
♫ I wake up

